    "negative_clarification": "Credit-claiming does NOT occur when the senator merely discusses, criticizes, or supports an issue, policy, or legislation without explicitly or implicitly tying their personal efforts to a specific achievement. This includes general statements of support, criticism of others' actions, or discussions of broader issues without a direct link to the senator's personal role in securing a result. Additionally, commemorative or ceremonial statements (e.g., honoring individuals or events) do not count as credit-claiming unless the senator explicitly ties their personal efforts to the outcome.",
